  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant will support veterinary inverventions for black and white rhinos in the South East lowveld of Zimbabwe for emergency health care and essential management operations in order to improve rhino security, monitoring of individuals and metapopulation management. The recipient will work with an experienced team to locate and immobilize rhinos when necessary in order to treat the animals for a) emergency veterinary treatment of snare injuries and other injuries, b) ear-notching and fitting horn implant transmitters to aid rhino monitoring, c) translocating rhinos in vulnerable areas to places of greater safety, d) dehorning to reduce poaching risk.</narrative>
  </description>
